# suite=video; columns: <FAULT_ID> <must-fail> <allowed-prefixes> <must-pass>
# Video named faults (plan 06-09, VID-03, D-13, D-15, D-16, A-06). Each id has one IVS_FAULT_<ID> site, in the owner TU named below, and
# is caught by the test it is named for; the allowed prefixes cover every collateral failure of the suite.
# VIDEO_STATE_DEPENDS_ON_BUFFER (core/src/stic/stic_frame.c): a frame completed with no video buffer does not advance the chain or the
# count, so the machine state depends on the presence of a buffer.
VIDEO_STATE_DEPENDS_ON_BUFFER video.noop.null-buffer video.noop. video.geom.profile-derives-159x96
# VIDEO_CHAIN_FRAMING_STRUCT_HASH (core/src/stic/stic_frame.c): the chain step hashes an image of a struct (host byte order, padding)
# instead of the framed big-endian header bytes.
VIDEO_CHAIN_FRAMING_STRUCT_HASH video.chain.framing-oracle video.chain. video.geom.profile-derives-159x96
# STIC_EVENT_ORDER_START_BEFORE_END (core/src/stic/stic_events.c): FRAME_START of the next frame (which clears the display decision) is
# applied before FRAME_END is rendered, so a displayed frame is delivered with its displayed flag clear.
STIC_EVENT_ORDER_START_BEFORE_END video.slot.displayed-flag-follows-latch video.slot.|video.frame. video.geom.profile-derives-159x96
